```java
// What @RestController means:
@Controller          // Registered as Spring bean, detected by component scan
@ResponseBody        // Every method return value → serialized to response body
public class UserController {}

// In practice:
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/users")
public class UserController {
    @GetMapping
    public List<User> getAll() {
        return userService.findAll(); // auto-serialized to JSON
    }
}
```

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/products")
public class ProductController {
    @GetMapping            // GET /api/products — list all
    @GetMapping("/{id}")   // GET /api/products/1 — get one
    @PostMapping           // POST /api/products — create new
    @PutMapping("/{id}")   // PUT /api/products/1 — full replace
    @PatchMapping("/{id}") // PATCH /api/products/1 — partial update
    @DeleteMapping("/{id}")// DELETE /api/products/1 — delete
}
```

```java
// On method — always return 201 Created
@PostMapping
@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
public User createUser(@RequestBody User user) {
    return userService.save(user); // returns 201, not 200
}

// On exception class — auto-maps exception to 404
@ResponseStatus(value = HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, reason = "User not found")
public class UserNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public UserNotFoundException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
// Throwing UserNotFoundException from any controller → 404 response automatically
```

**The problem**: React app on `http://localhost:3000` calls API on `http://localhost:8080`. Browser blocks this — different origin (port).

```java
// Allow specific origin on controller
@CrossOrigin(origins = "http://localhost:3000")
@RestController
public class UserController { ... }

// Or globally in WebMvcConfigurer:
@Override
public void addCorsMappings(CorsRegistry registry) {
    registry.addMapping("/api/**")
        .allowedOrigins("http://localhost:3000", "https://myapp.com")
        .allowedMethods("GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE")
        .allowCredentials(true);
}
```

